n, use explicit facts, explain why evidence supports or weakens candidate.\n\nWe are Agent 1. Our current vote is Candidate D per earlier. We need to decide whether to keep or change based on Agent 2's points. We can either maintain D, argue that D's strengths outweigh B's interpersonal flaw, or shift to B. Let's evaluate: D's strengths: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, handling unexpected events. Concerns: arrogant, hot temper, know-it-all, weak leadership. B's strengths: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concerns: grumpy, uncooperative, makes nasty remarks. Both have interpersonal concerns. Which is more severe? D's arrogance and hot temper could affect crew cooperation heavily. B's nasty remarks also harmful. Need to compare.\n\nWe can argue that D's operational strengths (responsibility, problem solving, concentration) are more critical for long-distance flights than B's technical skills, and that D's interpersonal issues, while concerning, may be mitigated with training, whereas B's uncooperative attitude is more entrenched (grumpy, uncooperative). Or we could shift to B.\n\nGiven the panel hasn't discussed A and C yet, but we need to compare D vs B now. We can keep D but ask for more info on B's crew cooperation. Or we can shift to B.\n\nWe need to provide a public message with a vote. Let's decide to keep D but note that we need more evidence on B's crew cooperation. However the instruction says each turn should include a vote. So we can keep D.\n\nWe'll say: I still recommend D because his responsibility, problem solving, concentration, and handling unexpected events directly address core safety criteria, and while his arrogance and hot temper are concerns, B also shows uncooperative behavior and nasty remarks, which may be equally detrimental. Therefore D remains the stronger overall fit.\n\nProvide explicit facts: D takes responsibility seriously, solves problems extremely well, concentrates very well, responds to unexpected events adequately. Concerns: arrogant, hot temper, know-it-all, weak leadership. B: very conscientious, handles stress well, but makes nasty remarks, can be uncooperative.\n\nExplain why D still preferred.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate D\"."}
